From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: stop pinning 44.1 kHz playback to 48000

sc8280xp_be_hw_params_fixup() runs on every backend link and opens with

	rate->min = rate->max = 48000;

so even once a DAI advertises 44100, the backend is moved to 48000 and
the DSP resamples. Widening the DAI masks alone therefore buys nothing:
it relocates the resample from PipeWire into the DSP.

Most of what this device plays is 44.1 kHz. The Dreamcast's AICA, the
PS1 SPU and the PSP all run at it and none has a 48 kHz mode.

The incoming rate is captured before the pin and restored for the two
playback ports that can carry it, PRIMARY_MI2S_RX and
RX_CODEC_DMA_RX_0, and only when the frontend asked for exactly 44100.
Every other backend keeps the pin, which matters most for
DISPLAY_PORT_RX_0: its DAI offers 48000, 96000 and 192000 only, so a
44.1 stream reaching it would fail. Capture is untouched, as are the
format and channel fixups.
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
@@ -76,6 +76,7 @@
 	struct snd_interval *channels = hw_param_interval(params,
 					SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_CHANNELS);
 	struct snd_mask *fmt = hw_param_mask(params, SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_FORMAT);
+	unsigned int fe_rate = rate->min;
 
 	rate->min = rate->max = 48000;
 	snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S16_LE);
@@ -88,6 +89,20 @@
 	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_3:
 		channels->min = 1;
 		break;
+	case PRIMARY_MI2S_RX:
+	case RX_CODEC_DMA_RX_0:
+		/*
+		 * Most of what this device plays is 44.1 kHz: the Dreamcast's
+		 * AICA, the PS1 SPU and the PSP all run at it and have no
+		 * 48 kHz mode. Pinning the backend to 48000 makes the DSP
+		 * resample every one of them. Let 44.1 through on the two
+		 * playback ports that can carry it, and leave every other
+		 * backend pinned - DISPLAY_PORT_RX_0 in particular offers
+		 * only 48000, 96000 and 192000.
+		 */
+		if (fe_rate == 44100)
+			rate->min = rate->max = 44100;
+		break;
 	default:
 		break;
 	}
